00:26:19.890 --> 00:26:39.400
<v Ira Glass>It's This American Life . I'm Ira Glass. This week on our show, Man vs. History, the stories of individuals taking action themselves during big historic moments. We've arrived at act two of our program. Act Two, Wenceslas Square. We have this short story about the final days of the Cold War from Arthur Phillips.
<v Ira Glass>这是《美国生活》。我是 Ira Glass。本周在我们的节目“人与历史”中，讲述的是个人在重大历史时刻采取行动的故事。我们已经进入了节目的第二幕。第二幕，瓦茨拉夫广场。我们有一个关于冷战最后日子的短篇故事，来自 Arthur Phillips。

00:26:39.400 --> 00:27:02.740
<v Arthur Phillips>In October of 1988, Tyler Vanalden received his second CIA posting, his first in the Communist bloc. He was dispatched to Prague, Czechoslovakia posing as a State Department third secretary in the US embassy. Eight weeks after his arrival in Prague, Tyler was standing at the cramped and decaying bar cafe he visited for an hour or so after work most days where he could practice a little Czech.
<v Arthur Phillips>1988 年 10 月，Tyler Vanalden 收到了他的第二个中情局派遣任务，这是他第一次被派往共产主义集团。他被派往捷克斯洛伐克布拉格，冒充美国大使馆的一名国务院三等秘书。抵达布拉格八周后，Tyler 站在一家局促且破败的酒吧咖啡馆里，他每天下班后通常会去那里待一小时左右，在那里他可以练习一点捷克语。

00:27:02.740 --> 00:27:22.810
<v Arthur Phillips>It was a Friday. The room was filling up and growing noisy with talk and music. Tyler looked up. Across the room, a beautiful young woman with short, blond hair was staring at him. She held his eye for a moment, then turned away, bit her lip, lit a cigarette with a shaking hand.
<v Arthur Phillips>那是周五。房间里挤满了人，谈话声和音乐声喧闹起来。Tyler 抬起头。房间对面，一位美丽的年轻女子，短金发，正盯着他看。她和他对视了片刻，然后移开目光，咬着嘴唇，用颤抖的手点燃了一支香烟。

00:27:22.810 --> 00:27:48.110
<v Arthur Phillips>"What made you suspicious?" his CIA supervisor Ed Marshall asked Tyler nine hours later in a dawn meeting back at the embassy. "You're a good looking guy. It could have been real." "No," said Tyler, "she looked a lot like a girl I went out with in college. When I first saw her I really thought it was her for a second. There's a picture of us in the yearbook kissing at a hockey game. And the little tattoo on her neck. You could see it in the picture."
<v Arthur Phillips>“什么让你产生怀疑？”他的中情局主管 Ed Marshall 九小时后在使馆的晨会上问 Tyler。“你是个帅小伙子。那可能是真的。”“不，”Tyler 说，“她看起来很像我在大学时交往的一个女孩。当我第一次见到她时，有那么一瞬间我真的以为是她。毕业纪念册里有我们在一场曲棍球比赛中接吻的照片。还有她脖子上的小纹身。你在照片里能看到。”

00:27:48.110 --> 00:28:10.050
<v Arthur Phillips>"And your new friend, this--" Ed examined his notes. "This Jarmila has a tattoo on her neck?" "And the same haircut," Tyler said. "You look as sad as I feel," said the girl in not bad English, 20 uncertain minutes after he first saw her. "Will you join me for a drink?"
<v Arthur Phillips>“而你的新朋友，这位——”Ed 检查了他的笔记。“这位 Jarmila 脖子上有纹身？”“发型也一样，”Tyler 说。“你看上去和我一样悲伤，”那个女孩用还不错的英语说，在他第一次见到她 20 分钟后，那是一段不确定的时间。“你能陪我喝一杯吗？”

00:28:10.050 --> 00:28:37.850
<v Arthur Phillips>Closer, she didn't really look much like Kim Wilsey , Tyler's happy, wholesome psych-major girlfriend for a few months of his senior year at Colby until she dumped him for being, quote, "emotionally unavailable, artificial, perfect, untouchable, impenetrable, affectless." But the Czech girl looked similar enough to attract him. She ran the tips of her fingers over her tattoo and said she was embarrassed by her poor English.
<v Arthur Phillips>凑近看，她其实不太像 Kim Wilsey，Tyler 在 Colby 大学的最后一年曾与之交往几个月的那个快乐、健康、心理学专业的女朋友，直到她甩了他，称他“情感疏离、虚假、完美、不可触碰、难以捉摸、无动于衷”。但这个捷克女孩看起来很像，足以吸引他。她用指尖划过纹身，说她因为英语不好而感到尴尬。

00:28:37.850 --> 00:29:00.900
<v Arthur Phillips>"You are from USA. What is it like there? We are told some very strange things about USA," she said with a sad, ironic smile. She would like to visit the USA someday but this is surely not possible because-- she trails off. She's sad. Does the handsome diplomat Tyler know what it is like to be sad? To feel hopeless?
<v Arthur Phillips>“你来自美国。那里是什么样子？有人告诉我们关于美国的一些非常奇怪的事情，”她带着一种悲伤、讽刺的微笑说。她希望有一天能去美国看看，但这肯定是不可能的，因为——她没说下去。她很难过。这位英俊的外交官 Tyler 知道难过是什么感觉吗？知道绝望是什么感觉吗？

00:29:00.900 --> 00:29:11.080
<v Arthur Phillips>"Yes, I have known this," he says in slightly poorer Czech than he can actually speak. "I would like to help you if I can."
<v Arthur Phillips>“是的，我经历过，”他用比他实际能说的更差一点的捷克语说。“如果可以的话，我想帮你。”

00:29:11.080 --> 00:29:32.850
<v Arthur Phillips>Her boyfriend has beaten her, she whispers. Tyler looks duly horrified, though he nearly laughs at this excessive, almost baroque ornamentation. "I would like," she whispers so low that Tyler has to lean close and place his ear next to her lips, "to escape from Czechoslovakia somehow and from Igor."
<v Arthur Phillips>她的男朋友打过她，她低语道。Tyler 看起来适时地感到恐惧，尽管他差点因为这种夸张、近乎巴洛克式的装饰而笑出来。“我想要，”她低声说道，声音低到 Tyler 不得不凑近并将耳朵贴在她的嘴唇旁，“以某种方式逃离捷克斯洛伐克，逃离 Igor。”

00:29:32.850 --> 00:30:00.880
<v Arthur Phillips>She pours wine for them both. "You are most beautiful girl I think to seeing in my whole life," Tyler muttered in clumsy Czech. "Nice," said Ed Marshall, not looking up from his note taking. "Was that true, by the way?" "No. She's cute, nothing special," Tyler lied unnecessarily even as he wondered why.
<v Arthur Phillips>她为他们俩倒了酒。“你是我这辈子见过的最美的女孩，”Tyler 用笨拙的捷克语嘟囔道。“不错，”Ed Marshall 说，没从记录笔记中抬头。“顺便问一下，那是真的吗？”“不是。她很可爱，没什么特别的，”Tyler 不必要地撒了谎，尽管他想知道为什么。

00:30:00.880 --> 00:30:17.390
<v Arthur Phillips>After almost two hours, a significant silence sat between them until she said, "Do you want to kiss me?" "More than anything I've ever wanted ever." She placed her soft lips on his just long enough for him to taste a drop of her wine. She pulled back hastily.
<v Arthur Phillips>在大约两小时后，一种显著的沉默存在于他们之间，直到她说，“你想吻我吗？”“比我这一辈子想要任何东西都更想。”她把柔软的嘴唇贴在他嘴唇上，时间刚好够他尝到一滴她的酒。她匆忙地退开了。

00:30:17.390 --> 00:30:42.630
<v Arthur Phillips>"Oh dear God what time it is." She wrenched her head to look at the clock behind her on the stained, brown and white wall and executed a flawless Cinderella. "I am so late. He will know. He will ask me. Oh Tyler, don't forget me. Please, you are so good and I so much need something good." A flustered gathering of her things, a momentary hand on his cheek, and out the door she ran in tearful panic.
<v Arthur Phillips>“哦，天哪，现在几点了。”她猛地转过头看向身后的棕白相间的脏墙上的时钟，像灰姑娘一样执行了一个完美的动作。“我迟到了。他会知道的。他会问我的。哦 Tyler，别忘了我。求你了，你人真好，我太需要一点美好的东西了。”她慌乱地收拾东西，一只手瞬间划过他的脸颊，然后泪流满面地惊慌跑出了门。

00:30:42.630 --> 00:30:53.330
<v Arthur Phillips>"And you boiled with desire," said Ed Marshall. "Yep," said Tyler. "And felt conspicuous. And got stuck with the tab."
<v Arthur Phillips>“而你内心欲望沸腾，”Ed Marshall 说。“是的，”Tyler 说。“而且感到引人注目。还得付账单。”

00:30:53.330 --> 00:31:20.630
<v Arthur Phillips>That afternoon, a second meeting with a larger team was held in a secure room at the embassy. They worked up a plan. She would surface again, no question. And when she did, Tyler would churn with contradictions. Relieved she's OK, but his pride injured that she ran off. Infatuated, but cautious. When alcohol entered the scene, he would slowly repeat that he hated his job. The US was a mess, politics a joke, blah blah blah.
<v Arthur Phillips>那天下午，与一个更大的团队在使馆的一个安全房间召开了第二次会议。他们制定了一个计划。她肯定会再次出现，毫无疑问。而当她出现时，Tyler 会在矛盾中挣扎。庆幸她没事，但又为她跑掉而自尊受损。迷恋，但又谨慎。当酒精介入时，他会慢慢重复他讨厌他的工作。美国一团糟，政治是个笑话，巴拉巴拉。

00:31:20.630 --> 00:31:41.660
<v Arthur Phillips>Every night for a week, Tyler returned to drink at The Wounded Bear. Seven nights, giving up later each night, dribbling smaller and smaller tips behind him. Night eight, December 14, 1988. She appears, very late, after Tyler has apparently drunk quite a bit alone in the noisy crowd.
<v Arthur Phillips>连续一周的每个晚上，Tyler 都回到“受伤的熊”酒吧喝酒。七个晚上，每天都走得越来越晚，留下的消费也越来越少。第八晚，1988 年 12 月 14 日。她出现了，很晚，在 Tyler 明显在嘈杂的人群中独自喝了不少酒之后。

00:31:41.660 --> 00:32:05.890
<v Arthur Phillips>"Oh thank God," she murmurs as she slides next to him. "I hoped, Tyler, but I did not dare to dream." He pulls away from her. She apologizes. He pouts. "Do not be like that please." "Then how should I be?" "If only you knew what Igor was like you would not be cruel to me. I thought you were different. So this is how you are."
<v Arthur Phillips>“哦，谢天谢地，”她溜到他身边时低声说。“我曾希望，Tyler，但我不敢梦想。”他推开了她。她道歉。他生气。“别那样，求你了。”“那我该怎样？”“如果你知道 Igor 是什么样的人，你就不会对我这么残忍了。我以为你是不同的。原来你是这样。”

00:32:05.890 --> 00:32:21.800
<v Arthur Phillips>She stands and leaves again. This time though, he swears aloud, drops money on the table, runs after her. He reaches her outside on the cobbled street, the snow just starting to turn heavy. He grabs her arm, turns her towards him. He tries to kiss her.
<v Arthur Phillips>她站起来又要走。但这次，他大声咒骂，扔下钱在桌上，追了出去。他在鹅卵石街道上追上了她，雪刚开始下得大起来。他抓住她的手臂，把她转向自己。他试图吻她。

00:32:21.800 --> 00:32:37.190
<v Arthur Phillips>"Have you gone mad?" she hisses in terror, pulls away. "We must not be seen together." And she glides over the snow into an alley. He has her tightly now. "My God you are such a handsome," she whispers. "But Igor--"
<v Arthur Phillips>“你疯了吗？”她在恐惧中嘶嘶地说，退开了。“我们不能被看见在一起。”她滑进雪地里的一条小巷。他紧紧抓住她。“天哪，你真帅，”她低语道。“但是 Igor——”

00:32:37.190 --> 00:32:57.780
<v Arthur Phillips>Igor is cruel, a weasel, a wolf of a man. He terrifies her. She thinks he's having her watched, perhaps even right now. If only she could think of how to be free of him. "I'll kill him," boasted engorged Tyler Vanalden. "I have diplomatic immunity." "Oh dear heaven, God no. He's powerful. He works for--"
<v Arthur Phillips>Igor 是残忍的，一个黄鼠狼，一个像狼一样的男人。他让她恐惧。她认为他在监视她，甚至可能就是现在。如果她能想到如何摆脱他就好了。“我会杀了他，”热血沸腾的 Tyler Vanalden 吹嘘道。“我有外交豁免权。”“哦，亲爱的上帝，不。他很强大。他为——工作。”

00:32:57.780 --> 00:33:03.470
<v Arthur Phillips>"Of course he does," said Marshall the next morning. "Bless his heart."
<v Arthur Phillips>“当然他是，”Marshall 第二天早上说。“祝福他的心。”

00:33:03.470 --> 00:33:26.670
<v Arthur Phillips>Weasel Igor worked for some vague division of the secret police. Jarmila certainly didn't know its name or where it was, only that Igor's job was to find out secrets about foreigners working in Czechoslovakia. And she simply could not think of how to escape his violent and lustful embrace described in increasing moist detail. She would go anywhere with Tyler if only she knew she was free and safe.
<v Arthur Phillips>黄鼠狼 Igor 为秘密警察的一个模糊部门工作。Jarmila 当然不知道它的名字或地址，只知道 Igor 的工作是找出在捷克斯洛伐克工作的外国人的秘密。而她根本无法想到如何逃离他那被描述得越来越潮湿的暴力和淫荡的拥抱。如果她知道自己是自由且安全的，她会跟 Tyler 去任何地方。

00:33:26.670 --> 00:34:12.840
<v Arthur Phillips>His kiss makes her bold. She will meet him. Enough of fear. She whispers an address and a time next Monday night, her friend's apartment. "For God's sake, be discreet going there. I have an idea," she says, "but I am afraid to ask you." "Ask me anything. Anything at all," he says. If you could bring me something to show Igor. Nothing really of value. I don't care what it is, a box of paper clips with your ambassador's name on them, then maybe I'm thinking, I can make Igor think I'm useful. I will not tell him about you of course. I am so frightened of him." She trembled. She kissed him. "Until Monday," she sobbed. And off she ran looking all around in fear.
<v Arthur Phillips>他的吻使她变得大胆。她会见他。不再恐惧。她低声说出了下周一晚上的地址和时间，她朋友的公寓。“看在上帝的份上，去那儿要谨慎。我有个主意，”她说，“但我不敢问你。”“问我任何事。任何事都可以，”他说。“如果你能带给我一些东西给 Igor 看。没什么真正的价值。我不在乎是什么，一盒写着你们大使名字的曲别针，那么也许我在想，我可以让 Igor 认为我有用。我当然不会告诉他关于你的事。我太怕他了。”她颤抖着。她吻了他。“周一见，”她抽泣着。然后她带着惊恐跑开了，四处张望。

00:34:12.840 --> 00:34:37.960
<v Arthur Phillips>"So who is this traitor, Tyler Vanalden?" Ed Marshall asks Tyler and the team. Tyler, they decided, is eager to please her but still wary of doing any real harm, more out of habit than principle. And so he has photocopied the personal information page from his nominal state department boss's file. Nothing much more than you could find in Washington, DC phone book, but plainly stamped confidential.
<v Arthur Phillips>“那么这个叛徒 Tyler Vanalden 是谁？”Ed Marshall 问 Tyler 和团队。他们认为 Tyler 急于取悦她，但仍对造成任何真正的伤害保持警惕，这更多是出于习惯而非原则。于是他复印了他名义上的国务院老板文件中的个人信息页。没什么比你在华盛顿特区电话簿里能找到的更多的了，但清晰地盖上了“机密”字样。

00:34:37.960 --> 00:34:50.990
<v Arthur Phillips>This first stolen document was prepared. How Vanalden had procured it was determined. His attitude to his lover for Monday was debated and decided. Bits of pivotal dialogue were drafted and rehearsed.
<v Arthur Phillips>第一份被盗文件准备好了。Vanalden 如何弄到它的过程已经确定。他周一对情人的态度已经辩论并决定。关键对话的片段已经起草并排练。

00:34:50.990 --> 00:35:34.950
<v Arthur Phillips>"This is for you," said Tyler, panting, nervous, pushing the Syrian envelope into her hands when she opened the door of her friend's apartment. "No," she cried, letting the poisonous thing fall. "I do not care. I do not want to see it. It does not matter. Only you matter." And she pulled Tyler Vanalden onto an old mattress on the floor of the bear, unnecessarily under-heated room where, to the audible accompaniment of a cassette of Beatles songs in Czech, and the inaudible accompaniment of hidden video cameras, Tyler displayed a wide range of emotional turmoil, having passable sex with Jarmila Herbeck of the Czech intelligence service.
